  m_Name: Brewer On A Skewer
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::IngredientData
  _name: Brewer On A Skewer
  _spoilTime: 15
  _normalSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: f70101dd45b994675abb6e8b3ab01b4f, type: 3}
  _spoiledSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: b147962d2da03454ab9caef43e151a65, type: 3}
  _plateSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d181bf620ede64080892c4464f79170c, type: 3}
  _isSmallIngredient: 0
  _recipeBookDescriptionUnspoiled: A local delicacy on the streets of Verehn, attributed
    to its easy grab-and-go nature. Popular amongst factory workers trying to sneak
    in a quick bite during their 5-minute breaks. Vendors source their skewers from
    wherever they could, usually from the wooden beams of ruined homes. Some vendors
    advertise that they source their skewers from aristocratic houses, as a "small
    bite of nobility".
  _recipeBookDescriptionSpoiled: "It is quite a feat to spoil the ingredients of
    a skewer, but when done so, it yields a pungent flavor that appeals to a more
    daring slice of society. Fans describe \u201Can intoxicating feeling\u201D that
    emboldens them; it might be the fermented dough...or something more sinister."
